--- /dev/null
+++ b/_bmad-output/specs/spec-cicd/evidence/23/shared-tls-pr-body.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+On a fresh Linux SDK user profile, shared TLS setup failed before product hooks: the certificate CLI requires its export directory in SSL_CERT_DIR during trust, and NSS retains the CLI nickname when the same certificate is reimported. Configure the process environment before trust and reuse the exported PEM basename for both NSS imports and checks. Preserve the prior environment on failure and publish it to later Actions steps only after all trust checks succeed.
+
+Validation: both new regressions reproduce their prior failures; all 16 prerequisite tests pass on Python 3.12 and 3.14. A fresh Ubuntu 26.04 / SDK 11.0.100 container passes the exact runtime, shared APT and TLS prerequisite probe, including both NSS databases and final certificate validation. Full Tenants integration and hosted acceptance remain separate gates.
